/-- **Exact CM discriminants** (README "Results").  For every curve in
`dkCerts`, `DkCert.Statement` holds: `q + 1 − t = h·n`; `t² − 4q = D_K·f²`;
`4q − t²` is the product of the certificate's prime powers; the odd-exponent
primes multiply to the squarefree part `s`, and `D_K = −s` (`D_K ≡ 1 mod 4`) or
`D_K = −4s` (`−s ≡ 2, 3 mod 4`); `D_K` is a discriminant; the recorded degree is
`min_nonscalar_degree(D_K)`, with `2^L ≤ |D_K| < 2^(L+1)` and degree `≥ 2^(L−2)`;
and IF the listed factors above 10^8 are prime (PARI `isprime`, not proved
here), `D_K` is fundamental.  Moreover, on all 7 curves `|D_K| ≥ 2^385` and every non-scalar element
of the order of discriminant `D_K` has norm `≥ 2^383`
(`Discriminant.minNonscalarDegree_isLeast`). -/
theorem exact_discriminants :
    dkCerts.length = 7 ∧
    (∀ c ∈ dkCerts, c.Statement) ∧
    (∀ c ∈ dkCerts, 2 ^ 385 ≤ c.DK.natAbs ∧ (2 : Int) ^ 383 ≤ c.deg) := by
  refine ⟨rfl, ?_, by decide +kernel⟩
  intro c hc
  simp only [dkCerts, List.mem_cons, List.not_mem_nil, or_false] at hc
  rcases hc with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl

  · exact nums_numsp384d1_certificate
  · exact other_Curve41417_certificate
  · exact nums_ed_510_mont_certificate
  · exact other_M_511_certificate
  · exact nums_numsp512d1_certificate
  · exact other_E_521_certificate
  · exact arkworks_ed_on_mnt4_753_certificate

